# Module Responsibilities

## LanguageDetector

Detects whether the input is Arabic or English.

Input

```
محمد احمد
```

Output

```
Arabic
```

---

## NameNormalizer

Normalizes text before processing.

### Arabic

Converts

```
أ
إ
آ
```

to

```
ا
```

Converts

```
ة
```

to

```
ه
```

Converts

```
ى
```

to

```
ي
```

Removes

- Tashkeel
- Tatweel
- Extra spaces

---

### English

- Lowercase
- Trim
- Remove duplicate spaces
- Remove punctuation if configured

Example

```
MOHAMED
```

↓

```
mohamed
```

---

# NameSplitter

Splits names into parts.

Example

```
Mohamed Ahmed Ali
```

↓

```
[
  Mohamed,
  Ahmed,
  Ali
]
```

---

# DictionaryService

Contains known names.

Example

```
Mohamed

↓

محمد
```

Dictionary lookup is always attempted before transliteration.

This produces much higher accuracy.

---

# Transliterator

Converts unknown names.

Example

```
Sherif

↓

شريف
```

Uses two rule sets.

## Multi-letter Rules

Always processed first.

Examples

```
sh → ش
kh → خ
gh → غ
th → ث
dh → ذ
oo → و
ee → ي
ou → و
ph → ف
ch → تش
```

---

## Single Letter Rules

Example

```
a → ا
b → ب
c → ك
d → د
...
```

---

# Candidate Generator

The most important component.

Input

```
Mohamed
```

Output

```
[
Mohamed,
Mohammad,
Muhammad,
Mohamad,
Muhammed,
محمد
]
```

Example

```
عبد الرحمن
```

↓

```
[
عبد الرحمن,
عبدالرحمن,
Abdelrahman,
Abdel Rahman,
Abdulrahman,
Abdurrahman
]
```

Instead of returning one translation, the engine returns all possible spellings.

---

# Search Repository

Instead of searching

```sql
WHERE Name = 'Mohamed'
```

Search

```sql
WHERE Name IN (...)
```

Example

```
[
محمد,
Mohamed,
Mohammad,
Muhammad
]
```

---

# Similarity Service

Ranks results.

Possible algorithms

- Levenshtein Distance
- Jaro-Winkler
- Dice Coefficient
- Cosine Similarity

Example

User types

```
Mohamad
```

Database

```
Mohamed
```

Similarity

```
97%
```

Result returned.

