# Long-Term Vision

The Search Dual Languages Engine should evolve beyond simple transliteration into a multilingual search platform. The engine will support multiple language pairs (e.g., English ↔ Arabic, English ↔ French, English ↔ Greek) through configurable language profiles while keeping the same pipeline of detection, normalization, candidate generation, and ranking.

Each supported language pair will contribute:
- Language detection rules.
- Normalization rules.
- Transliteration mappings.
- Common-name dictionaries.
- Phonetic encoding strategies.

This architecture allows new languages to be added without modifying the core search engine, making SDLE a reusable component for multilingual applications rather than a solution limited to English and Arabic.